Mutable bindings are `var`, not `let mut`; reassignment uses plain `=`.

```tuo
fn power(take base: Int, take exp: Int) -> Int {
    var result = 1;
    var i = 0;
    while i < exp {
        result = result * base;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    result
}

spec power {
    then power(2, 0) == 1;
    then power(2, 10) == 1024;
    then power(5, 3) == 125;
}
```

```tuo
fn sum(take xs: [Int; 5]) -> Int {
    var total = 0;
    for x in xs {
        total = total + x;
    }
    total
}

spec sum {
    then sum([1, 2, 3, 4, 5]) == 15;
    then sum([0; 5]) == 0;
}
```

`[0; 5]` is the repeat literal (five zeros). Array length is part of the type: `[Int; 5]` and `[Int; 4]` are different types.

